} Seed Map ({version}) — Biome \u0026 Structure Finder\",\"metaDescription\":\"Explore any Minecraft {label} seed on an interactive map — biomes, structures and ores, with measured accuracy shown for most structure markers. Updated for {siteVersion}, {editions}.\",\"h1Version\":\"Minecraft {line} Seed Map\",\"h1Edition\":\"Minecraft {label} Seed Map\",\"ogTitle\":\"Minecraft {label} Seed Map\",\"badge\":\"Supports Minecraft {platform} · {editions} · Updated {date}\",\"tldrVersion\":\"Yes — this seed map works for Minecraft {line}, in {editions}, updated {date}. {worldgen} Paste your seed and the map opens on {line} world generation, showing biomes, structures and ores; the table below shows the measured accuracy of each structure marker that has one.\",\"tldrEdition\":\"Yes — this seed map works for Minecraft {label} (current version {version}), updated {date}. {worldgen} Paste your seed and the map opens pinned to {label}, showing biomes, structures and ores; the table below shows the measured accuracy of each structure marker that has one.\",\"introHeading\":\"The Minecraft {label} seed map\",\"differsHeading\":\"How a Minecraft {label} world differs\",\"differsCountAll\":\"In a {label} world, this map shows all {total} structures it can find.\",\"differsCountSome\":\"In a {label} world, this map shows {available} of the {total} structures it can find; the table below says which.\",\"structureHeading\":\"Which structures generate in Minecraft {label}\",\"structureIntro\":\"“New in {line}” marks a structure Minecraft first generated in this version. The accuracy column is this map's measured accuracy for each structure, so a marker can occasionally be off; a dash means it has not been measured yet.\",\"colStructure\":\"Structure\",\"colStatus\":\"Generates in {line}?\",\"colAccuracy\":\"Accuracy\",\"statusNew\":\"New in {line}\",\"statusYes\":\"Yes\",\"statusAddedIn\":\"Added in {since}\",\"statusMapFrom\":\"Shown on this map from {since}\",\"statusNo\":\"Not in this version\",\"findLink\":\"Open the {feature} finder\",\"catalogLink\":\"{feature} reference\",\"faqHeading\":\"Minecraft {label} seed map — questions\",\"faqWorksQ\":\"Does this seed map work for Minecraft {label}?\",\"faqWorksA\":\"Yes. The map is pinned to Minecraft {label} the moment it loads, so you don't have to find the right version in a dropdown first. The table on this page shows the measured accuracy of each structure marker that has one.\",\"faqWorldgenQ\":\"What changed in Minecraft {line} world generation?\",\"faqWorldgenEditionQ\":\"Which world generation does the {label} seed map use?\",\"faqWorldgenA\":\"{worldgen}\",\"faqUpdatedQ\":\"What version is this seed map updated for?\",\"faqUpdatedA\":\"It supports Minecraft up to {version}. This page was last updated {date}.\",\"faqMatchQ\":\"Will my {label} seed match my in-game world?\",\"faqMatchA\":\"Usually, as long as the map's version matches the version your world was generated on. The measured accuracy of most structure markers is listed on this page, and a marker can occasionally be off. If a whole region looks wrong, the world was probably made on a different version; set the map to that version.\",\"comparisonHeading\":\"Version world-generation comparison\",\"comparisonIntro\":\"World generation changes in some Minecraft releases and not others. This table lists each version page and what it added, so you can pick the one your world was made on.\",\"comparisonColVersion\":\"Version\",\"comparisonColWorldgen\":\"Map opens on\",\"comparisonColEditions\":\"Editions\",\"comparisonColNew\":\"What's new\",\"comparisonNewNone\":\"—\",\"levelDatHeading\":\"Not sure which version made your world?\",\"levelDatBody\":\"Open your world's level.dat with the “Load save” button in the toolbar — the map reads the exact version and seed straight from the file, so you never have to guess which option to pick.\",\"browseHeading\":\"Browse other versions \u0026 editions\",\"browseIntro\":\"Same seed map, pinned to a different version or edition:\",\"viewerBacklink\":\"Open the full Minecraft seed map\",\"largeBiomes\":\"Made your world with the Large Biomes world type? In the map's version menu, choose Large Biomes, then {opensOn}. The seed stays the same, but the biomes come out much larger.\",\"editionsBoth\":\"Java + Bedrock\",\"editionsJava\":\"Java\",\"editionsBedrock\":\"Bedrock\"},\"1-21\":{\"worldgen\":\"1.21 (Tricky Trials) added Trial Chambers. This page opens on {opensOn}, the last release before 1.21.5 spread the Pale Garden into old Dark Forest land; if your world was made on another 1.21 release, pick that version in the map's version menu.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Trial Chambers\",\"differs\":\"1.21 added Trial Chambers, so a 1.21 world has them and a 1.20 world does not. The Pale Garden is not in every 1.21 world: it became part of normal worlds in 1.21.4, so a world made on 1.21 to 1.21.3 has none, and 1.21.5 spread it into old Dark Forest land, so the same seed shows it in more places from 1.21.5 on. If your world was made on any 1.21 release other than {opensOn}, pick that version in the map's version menu.\"},\"1-20\":{\"worldgen\":\"1.20 (Trails \u0026 Tales) generates on its own world-generation set, adding Cherry Groves and Trail Ruins to worlds made on this version.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Trail Ruins, Cherry Grove\",\"differs\":\"1.20 added Cherry Groves and Trail Ruins, so a 1.20 world has them and a 1.19 world does not. Trial Chambers came later, in 1.21, so a 1.20 world has none.\"},\"1-19\":{\"worldgen\":\"1.19 (The Wild Update) generates on its own set, adding the Deep Dark, Ancient Cities and the Mangrove Swamp.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Ancient Cities, Deep Dark, Mangrove Swamp\",\"differs\":\"1.19 added the Deep Dark, with Ancient Cities inside it, and the Mangrove Swamp, so a 1.19 world has them and a 1.18 world does not. It still has no Cherry Groves, Trail Ruins or Trial Chambers. This page opens on {opensOn}; for a world made on 1.19, 1.19.1 or 1.19.2, pick that version in the map's version menu.\"},\"1-18\":{\"worldgen\":\"1.18 (Caves \u0026 Cliffs Part II) rewrote terrain, cave and biome generation — the taller, deeper worlds every later version builds on.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Caves \u0026 Cliffs terrain\",\"differs\":\"1.18 rebuilt the terrain, caves and biomes, so the same seed gives different terrain and biomes here than on 1.17 or earlier, and every later version builds on this terrain. Next to later versions, a 1.18 world has no Deep Dark, Mangrove Swamps or Cherry Groves, and no Ancient Cities, Trail Ruins or Trial Chambers.\"},\"1-16\":{\"worldgen\":\"1.16 (the Nether Update) rebuilt the Nether with new biomes, Bastion Remnants and Nether Fossils on its own world-generation set.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Nether biomes, Bastion Remnants\",\"differs\":\"A 1.16 world comes from before 1.18 rebuilt the terrain, so the same seed gives different Overworld terrain and biomes here than on 1.18 or later. 1.16 brought the new Nether biomes and three structures: Bastion Remnants, Nether Fossils and Ruined Portals. This page opens on {opensOn}; worlds made on 1.16 or 1.16.1 generate parts of the Nether differently, so the map can be wrong for those two.\"},\"bedrock\":{\"worldgen\":\"Since 1.18, the same seed gives the same terrain and biomes on Bedrock as on Java, so the overworld here follows Java's generation for the matching release. Structure positions are computed with Bedrock's own placement, because those still differ between the editions.\",\"whatsNew\":\"Sulfur Caves biome\",\"differs\":\"Bedrock shares Java's terrain and biomes for the same seed since 1.18, but it places structures by its own rules, so villages, temples and strongholds stand in different spots than on any Java page, and strongholds do not form Java's rings. This page opens on Bedrock {opensOn}.\",\"mechanicsHeading\":\"Minecraft Bedrock seeds — what's different\",\"mechanicsSeedQ\":\"Do Bedrock and Java use the same seeds?\",\"mechanicsSeedA\":\"Yes. Since Bedrock 1.18.30, Bedrock world seeds are 64-bit whole numbers, the same range as Java (about -9.2 quintillion to 9.2 quintillion), so you can type the same seed into either edition without converting it. Bedrock before 1.18.30 used 32-bit seeds, which is why seeds from older guides are often small or negative numbers; they still work today. The same seed gives matching terrain and biomes on both editions, but structures are placed differently.\",\"mechanicsStructuresQ\":\"Do structures spawn in the same place on Bedrock and Java?\",\"mechanicsStructuresA\":\"No. Terrain and biomes match Java since 1.18, but structure placement uses different rules per edition, so villages, temples and strongholds sit in different spots. Strongholds in particular don't form the ring pattern Java uses.\"}},\"topToolbar\":{\"editionJava\":\"Java\",\"editionLargeBiomes\":\"Large Biomes\",\"editionBedrock\":\"Bedrock\",\"versionSectionLatest\":\"Latest\",\"versionSectionOld\":\"Old\",\"seedPlaceholder\":\"Enter seed...\",\"randomSeedTitle\":\"Generate random seed\",\"random\":\"Random\",\"loadTitle\":\"Load seed from Minecraft level.dat\",\"loading\":\"Loading…\",\"load\":\"Load\",\"dimensionOverworld\":\"Overworld\",\"dimensionNether\":\"Nether\",\"dimensionEnd\":\"End\",\"goToTitle\":\"Go to coordinates\",\"go\":\"Go!\",\"goToInvalid\":\"Enter numbers only.\",\"share\":\"Share\",\"shareTitle\":\"Share\",\"zoomInToShowMarkers\":\"Zoom in to show markers\",\"loadErrorMessage\":\"Couldn't read a seed from that file. Please choose a valid Minecraft level.dat and try again.\",\"versionAutoSwitched\":\"Switched to Java {version} to match your loaded world (was {previous}).\",\"seedHistoryTitle\":\"Saved \u0026 recent seeds\"},\"controlBar\":{\"terrain\":\"Terrain\",\"terrainToggleTitle\":\"Toggle terrain estimation\",\"topDown\":\"Top-down\",\"topDownToggleTitle\":\"Toggle the Top-down view\",\"grid\":\"Grid\",\"gridToggleTitle\":\"Toggle grid overlay\",\"advancedSettingsTitle\":\"Advanced se