px;height:24px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fmangrove-swamp.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fmangrove-swamp.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fmangrove-swamp.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75"/>Mangrove Swamp Finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/bamboo-jungle-finder"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:24px;height:24px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fbamboo-jungle.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fbamboo-jungle.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fbamboo-jungle.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75"/>Bamboo Jungle Finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/pale-garden-finder"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:24px;height:24px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fpale-garden.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fpale-garden.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fpale-garden.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75"/>Pale Garden Finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/sulfur-cave-finder"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:24px;height:24px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fsulfur-caves.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fsulfur-caves.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fbiome-icons%2Fsulfur-caves.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75"/>Sulfur Caves Finder</a></div><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/tools/biome-finder">Minecraft Biome Finder, all 60+ biomes</a></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s6" aria-labelledby="pb-s6-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1148px + -113.7 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 896px + -66.6 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 606px + -20.3 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 457px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 461px + 0 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s6-h">Coordinates, the Nether and the world border</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><div class="ms-pb-blks"><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Reading coordinates</h3><p>The line under the map follows your pointer: <strong>X</strong> across, <strong>Z</strong> up and down, and the biome you are over. In game, press F3 on Java, or switch coordinates on in Bedrock’s world settings, and you get the same three numbers. Open a marker and it hands you the exact X and Z plus a <code>/tp</code> line for chat.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Overworld to Nether: divide by eight</h3><p>One block in the Nether is eight in the Overworld. Divide your Overworld X and Z by 8 and that is where the other portal goes. Y stays the same. The map prints the matching Nether coordinate beside every one it hands you, so you never have to do the sum yourself.</p><div class="ms-pb-well"><span class="ms-pb-k">Overworld</span><span>X 1,600   Z 800</span><span class="ms-pb-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span><span class="ms-pb-k">Nether</span><span>X 200   Z 100</span></div></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Drawing a world border</h3><p>Switch the border on in Settings, set the middle and the radius, and the map draws the bit of world you can play in. A square, the shape Java’s <code>/worldborder</code> makes, or a circle. It counts the blocks across as you move around, and the copy button hands you both commands. Bedrock has no <code>/worldborder</code>, so there the border is for planning only.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s7" aria-labelledby="pb-s7-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1470px + -82.6 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 1166px + -19.1 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 1137px + -20.3 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 989px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 967px + 0 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s7-h">Minecraft Ore Finder</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><p>Tick an ore and the map lights up the chunks where it sits thickest, from the same seed the map is already drawing. One ore at a time, and each one carries its own number for the edition you picked.</p><div class="ms-pb-dtsc"><div class="ms-pb-dtp is-mid"><table class="ms-pb-dt"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ore</th><th scope="col" class="is-r">Java</th><th scope="col" class="is-r">Bedrock</th><th scope="col" class="is-r">Dig around</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fdiamond.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fdiamond.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fdiamond.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Diamond</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">88%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">87%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y −59</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fancient-debris.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fancient-debris.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fancient-debris.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Ancient Debris (Netherite)</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">91%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">85%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y 15</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Firon-ingot.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Firon-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Firon-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Iron</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">96%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">85%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y 16</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fgold-ingot.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fgold-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fgold-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Gold</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">83%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">92%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y −16</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcopper-ingot.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcopper-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcopper-ingot.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Copper</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">94%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">89%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y 48</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fredstone.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fredstone.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fredstone.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Redstone</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">93%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">93%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y −59</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Flapis-lazuli.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Flapis-lazuli.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Flapis-lazuli.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Lapis Lazuli</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">93%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">86%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y 0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="ms-pb-nm"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="object-contain" style="color:transparent;width:32px;height:32px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcoal.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcoal.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ffinder%2Fcoal.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75"/><strong>Coal</strong></span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">96%</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-est">Java only</span></td><td class="is-r"><span class="ms-pb-num">Y 96</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="ms-pb-fq"><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o0"><span>How does the Ore Finder work?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o0" hidden="">Tick the ore you want, set a Y range if you already know where you want to dig, and the map lights up the hotspots. A hotspot is a chunk where that ore sits thicker than usual, at the Y shown beside it. Head there, dig down to that Y and branch out a few blocks each way. Coal is Java only, diamond hotspots are a Supporter perk, and older versions hide their ore at other heights.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o1"><span>Why is it not always right?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o1" hidden="">The number beside each ore is how often a hotspot pays off. Most of them will have the ore waiting for you. A few will not, and a vein can sit a few blocks from the middle of the chunk, so dig around a bit before you move on to the next hotspot. Bedrock and older versions are a little less exact.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o2"><span>Which ores can the finder locate?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o2" hidden="">In the Overworld it finds diamond, iron, copper, gold, redstone, lapis lazuli and coal, and in the Nether it finds ancient debris (netherite). You search one ore at a time and can optionally limit the search to a specific Y level.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o3"><span>What is the best Y level to mine diamonds?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o3" hidden="">Diamonds get more common the deeper you dig, peaking around Y -59 in current versions (they generate between Y -64 and Y 16). The finder defaults to each ore&#x27;s full spawn range, and you can tick &#x27;limit to a specific Y level&#x27; to focus on the richest band – for diamonds, around Y -59 to -54.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o4"><span>Does the Ore Finder work for my Minecraft version?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o4" hidden="">It works on both Java and Bedrock Edition. On Java it covers modern versions, including 1.21 and the 26.x releases, which share the same ore-generation rules. Bedrock Edition is now supported as well – on 1.18 and newer it finds the Overworld ores (diamond, iron, copper, gold, redstone and lapis lazuli). The two editions use different world generators, so make sure you pick the edition your world was created in.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-o5"><span>Is using the Ore Finder cheating?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-o5" hidden="">That is up to how you like to play. In single-player it is just a faster version of strip-mining for a diamond start. On multiplayer servers, check the rules first – some servers don&#x27;t allow seed-based tools.</div></div></div><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/tools/ore-finder">Minecraft Ore Finder</a><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/tools/diamond-finder">Diamond Finder</a><span class="ms-pb-lk"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/blog/how-to-find-diamonds-in-minecraft">How to find diamonds in Minecraft — the full guide</a></span></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s8" aria-labelledby="pb-s8-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1762px + -173.9 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 1121px + -38.6 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 989px + -17.8 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 859px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 863px + 0 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s8-h">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><div class="ms-pb-fq"><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g1"><span>What is a Minecraft seed map?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g1" hidden="">It draws the world a Minecraft seed will make, before you ever load it: the biomes, and where the villages, strongholds, ancient cities and monuments will stand. Type the seed, pick your edition and version, and you get coordinates you can walk to. Nothing is downloaded; sign in and your saved seeds and pins sync to your account.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi is-op"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="pb-a-g2"><span>Is this seed map accurate?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g2">Open a marker and it tells you how often that thing really stands there, up to <strong>99%</strong>, for that structure in your edition. Villages, strongholds and monuments are the safest bets. A few things that move about with the ground around them say Estimate instead of a number. On Bedrock the numbers can sit a bit lower than on Java for the same seed.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g3"><span>How do I find the seed of my world?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g3" hidden="">In a Java single-player world, type <code>/seed</code> in chat; it works with cheats off. On Bedrock, read it off your world&#x27;s settings screen, no cheats needed. On a server or Realm, ask the owner for it. If you have the save folder, drop the Java <code>level.dat</code> on this page and the seed and version fill themselves in.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g4"><span>Are Java and Bedrock seeds the same?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g4" hidden="">No. Java Edition and Bedrock Edition use different world-generation algorithms, so the same seed produces completely different worlds in each edition. Always pick the matching edition before generating the map.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g5"><span>Which Minecraft versions does the map cover?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g5" hidden="">Java from 1.0 up to 26.3, Bedrock from 1.16 up to 1.26.60, and Large Biomes on top. Pick the exact version your world was made in. Minecraft changed the shape of its worlds at 1.13, 1.15 and 1.18, so a 1.12 world and a 1.18 world from the same seed look nothing alike.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g6"><span>How do I turn Overworld coordinates into Nether coordinates?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g6" hidden="">Divide by eight. One block in the Nether is eight in the Overworld, so Overworld X 1,600 and Z 800 is Nether X 200 and Z 100, and Y stays the same. The map prints the matching coordinate beside every one it hands you, so you never have to do the sum yourself.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g7"><span>How do I keep a seed so I can come back to it?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g7" hidden="">Press save on the toolbar, next to Share. The world you are looking at joins your seeds, with its edition and version. Press again to drop it. Signed out, they stay in this browser. Sign in with a free account and they follow you to every device.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g8"><span>How do I find slime chunks?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g8" hidden="">Switch on the slime-chunk layer and the map shades every chunk where slimes can spawn in the Overworld. Slime chunks come from the seed and the chunk, not from the biome. Below Y 40 they spawn at any light level. Swamps are the other place, and there it goes by light and moon phase.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g9"><span>How do I find a stronghold and the End portal?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g9" hidden="">Switch strongholds on and the map marks all of them. Open a marker for its coordinates and, where it is known, the End portal itself and how many eyes are already in the frame. Copy the <code>/tp</code> line from the marker. Strongholds sit deep, so expect to dig well below sea level.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g10"><span>Why does the map show a structure that isn&#x27;t in my world — and how do I fix it?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g10" hidden="">Almost always it is a version or edition mismatch. Java and Bedrock generate completely different worlds from the same seed, and even within one edition the structure layout changes across major updates. Check that the edition and the exact version selected above the map match the world you are playing, then regenerate. Some markers are chunk-centre approximations, so the real structure can sit a few blocks from the marker; and on rare occasions a marker fails to render, which reloading the page fixes.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g11"><span>Do my pins and kept seeds sync across devices?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g11" hidden="">On their own they stay in this browser. Make a free account, sign in, and your seeds, pins and ticked-off structures follow you to every device. The map works the same either way.</div></div><div class="ms-pb-fqi"><h3 class="ms-pb-fqh"><button type="button" class="ms-pb-fqq" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pb-a-g12"><span>Is using the Minecraft Seed Map considered cheating?</span><span class="ms-pb-cv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div class="ms-pb-fqa" id="pb-a-g12" hidden="">That is up to how you play. For exploring your own world, or hunting a biome for a build, most people are happy with it. On a server, read the rules first, because some do not allow seed tools.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s9" aria-labelledby="pb-s9-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1507px + -45.8 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 1326px + -7.2 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 1266px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 695px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 699px + 0 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s9-h">Biome names in Java vs Bedrock Edition</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><p>Bedrock still calls a fair few biomes by their old names. Pick Bedrock above the map and the biome list swaps over on its own, and the search box takes either name. Here is the whole lot.</p><div class="ms-pb-cols2"><div class="ms-pb-dtsc"><div class="ms-pb-dtp"><table class="ms-pb-dt"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Java Edition</th><th scope="col">Bedrock Edition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Snowy Beach</strong></td><td>Cold Beach</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Stony Shore</strong></td><td>Stone Beach</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dark Forest</strong></td><td>Roofed Forest</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Old Growth Birch Forest</strong></td><td>Birch Forest Mutated</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Windswept Forest</strong></td><td>Extreme Hills Plus Trees</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Ice Spikes</strong></td><td>Ice Plains Spikes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sparse Jungle</strong></td><td>Jungle Edge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Badlands</strong></td><td>Mesa</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Eroded Badlands</strong></td><td>Mesa Bryce</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Wooded Badlands</strong></td><td>Mesa Plateau</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="ms-pb-dtsc"><div class="ms-pb-dtp"><table class="ms-pb-dt"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Java Edition</th><th scope="col">Bedrock Edition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Windswept Gravelly Hills</strong></td><td>Extreme Hills Mutated</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Windswept Hills</strong></td><td>Extreme Hills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mushroom Fields</strong></td><td>Mushroom Island</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Snowy Plains</strong></td><td>Ice Plains</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Windswept Savanna</strong></td><td>Savanna Mutated</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Swamp</strong></td><td>Swampland</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Old Growth Pine Taiga</strong></td><td>Mega Taiga</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Old Growth Spruce Taiga</strong></td><td>Mega Spruce Taiga</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Snowy Taiga</strong></td><td>Cold Taiga</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nether Wastes</strong></td><td>Nether</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s10" aria-labelledby="pb-s10-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1943px + -216.2 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 1380px + -95.7 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 763px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 708px + -17.1 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 716px + -19.8 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s10-h">Map not matching your world?</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><p>When the map and your world disagree, it is nearly always one of these six.</p><div class="ms-pb-cols2"><div class="ms-pb-blks"><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Wrong seed or coordinates</h3><p>Double-check that the seed is typed exactly as in-game, with no leading or trailing spaces. Seeds are case-sensitive only when entered as text – numeric seeds must match exactly.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Edition or version mismatch</h3><p>Java Edition and Bedrock Edition generate completely different worlds for the same seed. Within a single edition, different Minecraft versions can also produce noticeably different terrain – especially across the major 1.13, 1.15 and 1.18 world-gen overhauls. Pick the edition and version that was used to generate the chunks you are looking at.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Mods, datapacks or world presets</h3><p>Mods, behaviour packs, datapacks and custom world presets can all change world generation. If your world uses any of these, the map may no longer be accurate for the modified areas.</p></div></div><div class="ms-pb-blks"><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Coastlines and terrain vs. biomes</h3><p>From version 1.18 onwards, coastlines do not match biome boundaries exactly. The seed map shows the underlying biomes, not the water level, so terrain that drops below sea level inside a land biome still appears in its land colour — a bay or lake can show up green. The opposite case, water colour over dry land, is rare. The terrain option shades the relief so those low areas stand out; on Java, zoomed in close, it also paints them as water.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Missing Y coordinates</h3><p>Some features such as mineshafts, strongholds and nether fortresses extend vertically, so a Y coordinate is only shown when it is meaningful. For buried structures, search at different heights at the given X/Z.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><h3>Slime chunks show no slimes in-game</h3><p>Slime chunks have a very low natural spawn rate. You may need to wait several minutes in a large, fully lit area, and make sure there are no other hostile mob spawns nearby competing for the mob cap.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s11" aria-labelledby="pb-s11-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1291px + -164.2 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 714px + -48.6 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 586px + -29.5 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 500px + -16 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 371px + -13 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s11-h">More Minecraft tools</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><div class="ms-pb-chips"><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/seed-finder"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21v-8M12 13c0-4-3-6-7-6 0 4 3 6 7 6zM12 13c0-4 3-6 7-6 0 4-3 6-7 6z"></path></svg>Minecraft Seed Finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/best-seeds"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l2.8 6 6.2.7-4.6 4.3 1.3 6.2L12 17l-5.7 3.2 1.3-6.2L3 9.7 9.2 9z"></path></svg>Best Minecraft Seeds</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/ore-finder"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 4v10l-7 4-7-4V7z M12 3v18M5 7l7 4 7-4"></path></svg>Ore Finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/structure-finder"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-6-5.5-6-11a6 6 0 0 1 12 0c0 5.5-6 11-6 11z M12 10.5h.01"></path></svg>Structure finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/biome-finder"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 20c0-8 5-14 14-14 0 9-6 14-14 14zM5 20l8-8"></path></svg>Biome finder</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/enchantment-planner"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h7a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H4zM20 4h-7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h7z"></path></svg>Enchantment Tool</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/command-generator"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 4h18v14H3zM7 8h.01M11 8h.01M15 8h.01M7 12h.01M11 12h.01M15 12h.01M8 16h8"></path></svg>Minecraft Command Generator</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/crafting-calculator"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 3h18v18H3zM3 9h18M3 15h18M9 3v18M15 3v18"></path></svg>Crafting Calculator</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/tools/text-studio"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 20l4-1 11-11-3-3L5 16zM13 6l3 3"></path></svg>Text Studio</a><a class="ms-map-chip ms-pb-chip" href="/"><svg class="ms-map-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 11m-6 0a6 6 0 1 0 12 0 6 6 0 1 0-12 0M20 20l-4.5-4.5"></path></svg>Items, blocks and mobs</a></div><span class="ms-map-kick">Read next</span><div class="ms-pb-frow"><span class="ms-pb-lk"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/blog/minecraft-seed-map-accuracy">How accurate are Minecraft seed maps?</a></span><span class="ms-pb-lk"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/blog/how-to-use-a-seed-map">How to use a seed map</a></span><span class="ms-pb-lk"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/blog/how-to-find-your-minecraft-seed">How to find your Minecraft seed</a></span><span class="ms-pb-lk"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/blog/how-to-find-diamonds-in-minecraft">How to find diamonds in Minecraft</a></span></div></div></section><section class="ms-pb-sec" id="pb-s12" aria-labelledby="pb-s12-h" style="--pb-h0:max(0px, 1346px + -94.2 * 1vw);--pb-h1:max(0px, 1075px + -36.1 * 1vw);--pb-h2:max(0px, 834px + 0 * 1vw);--pb-h3:max(0px, 744px + -17.1 * 1vw);--pb-h4:max(0px, 641px + -15.5 * min(1vw, 12.2px))"><div class="ms-pb-sh"><h2 id="pb-s12-h">Credits</h2></div><div class="ms-pb-sb"><p>The Minecraft Search seed map is built on top of outstanding open-source work by the wider Minecraft and web-tooling community. Huge thanks to the authors of the following projects:</p><div class="ms-pb-cols2"><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/Cubitect/cubiomes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cubiomes<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>Java Edition biome and structure generation, by Cubitect and contributors.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/reedacartwright/cubiomes/tree/bedrock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cubiomes (Bedrock fork)<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>Bedrock 1.16 and 1.17 biomes and Bedrock Nether generation, by Reed A. Cartwright.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/Earthcomputer/bedrockified" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bedrockified<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>Bedrock structure algorithms, by Earthcomputer.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/bedrock-dev/MCBEStructureFinder" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MCBEStructureFinder<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>Additional Bedrock structure generation logic, by xiaohengying.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/toolbox4minecraft/amidst" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Amidst<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>Biome colour palette reference.</p></div><div class="ms-pb-blk"><div class="ms-pb-frow"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="https://github.com/openlayers/openlayers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenLayers<svg class="ms-map-ico" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9M18 13v7H4V6h7"></path></svg></a></div><p>The map rendering engine.</p></div></div><p>Bedrock 1.16 and 1.17 biomes and Bedrock Nether are calculated using a cubiomes fork by Reed A. Cartwright.</p><p>Minecraft Search is not affiliated with Mojang Studios or Microsoft. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Studios.</p><p class="ms-pb-small"><a class="ms-map-popup-link ms-pb-link" href="/oss-licenses.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open-source license texts</a></p></div></section><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the Ore Finder work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tick the ore you want, set a Y range if you already know where you want to dig, and the map lights up the hotspots. A hotspot is a chunk where that ore sits thicker than usual, at the Y shown beside it. Head there, dig down to that Y and branch out a few blocks each way. Coal is Java only, diamond hotspots are a Supporter perk, and older versions hide their ore at other heights."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is it not always right?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The number beside each ore is how often a hotspot pays off. Most of them will have the ore waiting for you. A few will not, and a vein can sit a few blocks from the middle of the chunk, so dig around a bit before you move on to the next hotspot. Bedrock and older versions are a little less exact."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which ores can the finder locate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the Overworld it finds diamond, iron, copper, gold, redstone, lapis lazuli and coal, and in the Nether it finds ancient debris (netherite). You search one ore at a time and can optionally limit the search to a specific Y level."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best Y level to mine diamonds?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Diamonds get more common the deeper you dig, peaking around Y -59 in current versions (they generate between Y -64 and Y 16). The finder defaults to each ore's full spawn range, and you can tick 'limit to a specific Y level' to focus on the richest band – for diamonds, around Y -59 to -54."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the Ore Finder work for my Minecraft version?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It works on both Java and Bedrock Edition. On Java it covers modern versions, including 1.21 and the 26.x releases, which share the same ore-generation rules. Bedrock Edition is now supported as well – on 1.18 and newer it finds the Overworld ores (diamond, iron, copper, gold, redstone and lapis lazuli). The two editions use different world generators, so make sure you pick the edition your world was created in."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is using the Ore Finder cheating?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is up to how you like to play. In single-player it is just a faster version of strip-mining for a diamond start. On multiplayer servers, check the rules first – some servers don't allow seed-based tools."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a Minecraft seed map?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It draws the world a Minecraft seed will make, before you ever load it: the biomes, and where the villages, strongholds, ancient cities and monuments will stand. Type the seed, pick your edition and version, and you get coordinates you can walk to. Nothing is downloaded; sign in and your saved seeds and pins sync to your account."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this seed map accurate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Open a marker and it tells you how often that thing really stands there, up to 99%, for that structure in your edition. Villages, strongholds and monuments are the safest bets. A few things that move about with the ground around them say Estimate instead of a number. On Bedrock the numbers can sit a bit lower than on Java for the same seed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I find the seed of my world?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In a Java single-player world, type /seed in chat; it works with cheats off. On Bedrock, read it off your world's settings screen, no cheats needed. On a server or Realm, ask the owner for it. If you have the save folder, drop the Java level.dat on this page and the seed and version fill themselves in."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are Java and Bedrock seeds the same?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Java Edition and Bedrock Edition use different world-generation algorithms, so the same seed produces completely different worlds in each edition. Always pick the matching edition before generating the map."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Minecraft versions does the map cover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Java from 1.0 up to 26.3, Bedrock from 1.16 up to 1.26.60, and Large Biomes on top. Pick the exact version your world was made in. Minecraft changed the shape of its worlds at 1.13, 1.15 and 1.18, so a 1.12 world and a 1.18 world from the same seed look nothing alike."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I turn Overworld coordinates into Nether coordinates?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Divide by eight. One block in the Nether is eight in the Overworld, so Overworld X 1,600 and Z 800 is Nether X 200 and Z 100, and Y stays the same. The map prints the matching coordinate beside every one it hands you, so you never have to do the sum yourself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I keep a seed so I can come back to it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Press save on the toolbar, next to Share. The world you are looking at joins your seeds, with its edition and version. Press again to drop it. Signed out, they stay in this browser. Sign in with a free account and they follow you to every device."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I find slime chunks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Switch on the slime-chunk layer and the map shades every chunk where slimes can spawn in the Overworld. Slime chunks come from the seed and the chunk, not from the biome. Below Y 40 they spawn at any light level. Swamps are the other place, and there it goes by light and moon phase."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I find a stronghold and the End portal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Switch strongholds on and the map marks all of them. Open a marker for its coordinates and, where it is known, the End portal itself and how many eyes are already in the frame. Copy the /tp line from the marker. Strongholds sit deep, so expect to dig well below sea level."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does the map show a structure that isn't in my world — and how do I fix it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Almost always it is a version or edition mismatch. Java and Bedrock generate completely different worlds from the same seed, and even within one edition the structure layout changes across major updates. Check that the edition and the exact version selected above the map match the world you are playing, then regenerate. Some markers are chunk-centre approximations, so the real structure can sit a few blocks from the marker; and on rare occasions a marker fails to render, which reloading the page fixes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do my pins and kept seeds sync across devices?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On their own they stay in this browser. Make a free account, sign in, and your seeds, pins and ticked-off structures follow you to every device. The map works the same either way."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is using the Minecraft Seed Map considered cheating?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is up to how you play. For exploring your own world, or hunting a biome for a build, most people are happy with it. On a server, read the rules first, because some do not allow seed tools."}}]}</script></article><div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-3 pt-6 pb-2"><p class="mb-2.5 text-[15px] font-extrabold text-stone-200 [text-wrap:pretty]">The Seed Map in your pocket</p><div class="ms-stores"><a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6790169279" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-store="ios"><img src="/images/store-badges/ios-en-US.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" width="120" height="40" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.minecraftsearch.seedmap&amp;referrer=utm_source%3Dminecraftsearch.com%26utm_medium%3Dwebsite%26utm_campaign%3Dseed_map" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-store="android"><img src="/images/store-badges/play-en-US.png" alt="Get it on Google Play" width="134" height="40" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a></div></div></div></div></div><!--$--><!--/$--></div><script>$RC("B:3","S:3")</script><div hidden id="S:4"><footer class="DIsf9G_variable font-nunito border-t-[3px] border-[var(--face)] bg-[var(--g600)] shadow-[inset_0_3px_0_var(--hi)]"><div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[592px] flex-col gap-[24px] px-4 pb-[22px] pt-[28px] md:grid md:max-w-[1200px] md:grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(210px,1fr))] md:items-start md:gap-[26px] md:px-5 md:pb-[26px] md:pt-[30px]"><div clas